Permitted Purposes include:
- Internal use: running, testing, and developing automated test suites within any company, business, or commercial project.
- Professional services & outsourcing: using the Software to scaffold, build, test, and deliver projects for paying clients or third-party customers.
- Non-commercial education and research: academic coursework, training, hobby projects, and vulnerability research.

## 3. Competing Use

A Competing Use means using the Software in a commercial product or service that:
(a) substitutes for the Software;
(b) substitutes for any other product or service offered by the Licensor using the Software as of the date the Software was made available; or
(c) offers the same or substantially similar functionality as the Software.

